## How the documentation is organized

* @longshadow-4@Getting started@ covers things every app shares: looks, files, sharing, offline use and privacy!
* ++R#}Apps++ has one guide per app, written from the real buttons and tabs!
* ++Y-(Keydown++ is the full formatting language, including a reference of every tag, style and block!
* !!4PR#Languages# covers BitLang, Plume and the Suave programming language!
* ++C-Reference++ has the FAQ and troubleshooting!

Press `Ctrl+K`{key} (or `/`{key}) anywhere on this page to search all of it!

::divider{wavy|Three ideas to remember|blue}

## Three ideas to remember

1. @patch-2@Everything is Keydown.@ Documents, notes, slides, messages and wiki articles are all Keydown text, so a tag you learn in one app works in all of them!
2. @led-4@Files are yours.@ Apps save plain files you can open in other Radii apps, and every app can export what you made!
3. ++Y#)Looks are a switch.++ Every app has the same three layouts, so you can pick the one you like best, and your documents never change!

-# This site is itself written in Keydown and drawn with Dark Keydown, the version that fades to white instead of transparent so every style looks right on a dark page!
